---
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import { serviceAuth } from "../diagrams";
import Guide from "../layouts/Guide.astro";

const origin = process.env.EMDASH_SITE_URL || Astro.url.origin;
const siteDid = `did:web:${new URL(origin).host.replace(":", "%3A")}`;

const toc = [
	{ id: "sign-in", label: "Sign in" },
	{ id: "publish", label: "Publish records" },
	{ id: "connect", label: "Connect" },
	{ id: "run", label: "Run a module" },
	{ id: "cli", label: "From your terminal" },
	{ id: "own", label: "Your own integration" },
	{ id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting" },
];

const tools = `go install github.com/bluesky-social/goat@latest
git clone https://github.com/publicdomainrelay/socialweb-computer-emdash
cd socialweb-computer-emdash
export ATPROTO_HANDLE=you.bsky.social ATPROTO_PASSWORD='your-app-password'`;

const publishRecords = `./scripts/publish-records.sh`;

const publishModules = `rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
./scripts/publish-wasm.sh statusphere
./scripts/publish-wasm.sh vibescrobble`;

const check = `goat record ls --collection com.fedfork.exec.oauth.clientMetadata "$ATPROTO_HANDLE"
goat record ls --collection com.fedfork.exec.wasm.module "$ATPROTO_HANDLE"`;

const cliSetup = `SITE=${origin}
SITE_DID=${siteDid}
DOC=$(goat resolve "$ATPROTO_HANDLE")
DID=$(jq -r .id <<<"$DOC")
PDS=$(jq -r '.service[] | select(.id == "#atproto_pds") | .serviceEndpoint' <<<"$DOC")
ACCESS_JWT=$(curl -fsS -X POST "$PDS/xrpc/com.atproto.server.createSession" \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d "{\\"identifier\\":\\"$ATPROTO_HANDLE\\",\\"password\\":\\"$ATPROTO_PASSWORD\\"}" | jq -r .accessJwt)`;

const viaProxy = `curl -fsS -X POST "$PDS/xrpc/com.fedfork.exec.wasm.run" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_JWT" \\
  -H "atproto-proxy: $SITE_DID#emdash_integrations" \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d "{\\"module\\":\\"at://$DID/com.fedfork.exec.wasm.module/statusphere\\",\\"entry\\":\\"set_status\\",\\"input\\":{\\"status\\":\\"🦋\\"}}" | jq .result`;

const viaToken = `TOKEN=$(curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_JWT" \\
  "$PDS/xrpc/com.atproto.server.getServiceAuth?aud=$SITE_DID&lxm=com.fedfork.exec.wasm.run" | jq -r .token)
curl -fsS -X POST "$SITE/xrpc/com.fedfork.exec.wasm.run" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d "{\\"module\\":\\"at://$DID/com.fedfork.exec.wasm.module/vibescrobble\\",\\"entry\\":\\"scrobble\\",\\"input\\":{\\"text\\":\\"🚀 deployed my own site\\"}}" | jq .result`;

const ownRecord = `{
  "$type": "com.fedfork.exec.oauth.clientMetadata",
  "name": "Example",
  "clientMetadata": {
    "client_id": "https://example.com/oauth-client-metadata.json",
    "client_uri": "https://example.com",
    "redirect_uris": ["https://example.com/oauth/callback"],
    "scope": "atproto repo:com.example.post repo:com.example.like"
  },
  "scopeGroups": [
    { "key": "posts", "label": "Write posts", "scopes": ["repo:com.example.post"] },
    { "key": "likes", "label": "Like posts", "scopes": ["repo:com.example.like"] }
  ],
  "createdAt": "2026-11-06T00:00:00.000Z"
}`;

const ownPublish = `goat lex validate -c lexicons example.json
goat record create -n -r example example.json`;
---

<Guide
	title="Use it"
	eyebrow="Guide"
	description="Sign in, put integration records in your PDS, connect them with the permissions you pick, and run their modules from the page or your terminal."
	toc={toc}
>
	<section id="sign-in">
		<h2>Sign in</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li>
				<strong>Open integrations</strong>
				Go to <a href="/integrations">/integrations</a> and enter your handle, for example <code>alice.bsky.social</code>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Approve on your PDS</strong>
				Your authorization server asks for the <code>atproto</code> scope only. It tells the site who you are, and nothing else.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>See your integrations</strong>
				The site lists the <code>com.fedfork.exec.oauth.clientMetadata</code> records in your repo. With none, the list is empty until you publish one.
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section id="publish">
		<h2>Publish records</h2>
		<p>
			The repo ships three integration records and two modules. Publish them to your own account with <a href="https://github.com/bluesky-social/goat">goat</a>. Use an app password, not your main password.
		</p>
		<Code code={tools} />
		<p>Publish the integration records in <code>records/</code>: statusphere, vibescrobble and socialweb-computer.</p>
		<Code code={publishRecords} />
		<p>Build and publish the modules. Each script builds with Cargo, uploads the blob, and writes a <code>wasm.module</code> record that points to its integration by URI and CID.</p>
		<Code code={publishModules} />
		<Code title="check" code={check} />
		<div class="callout tone-sandbox">
			<strong>Republish modules after their integration changes.</strong>
			A module record pins its integration record's CID. Run <code>publish-records.sh</code> first, then <code>publish-wasm.sh</code>.
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="connect">
		<h2>Connect</h2>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li>
				<strong>Tick scope groups</strong>
				Each card lists the record's permission groups. Tick only what you want this site to do.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Connect</strong>
				You go to your authorization server again, this time for those scopes. Approve and you come back to <code>/integrations?connected=…</code>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Verify or change</strong>
				<em>Verify</em> calls <code>getSession</code> with the session and shows its handle and scopes. Tick more groups and press <em>Update permissions</em> to add scopes. <em>Disconnect</em> revokes the session.
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section id="run">
		<h2>Run a module</h2>
		<p>Connected cards show their modules. Fill the fields and press the action.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Statusphere.</strong> <em>Set status</em> takes one emoji and writes an <code>xyz.statusphere.status</code> record. Setting the same emoji again returns <code>unchanged</code>. <em>Clear statuses</em> deletes your status records.</li>
			<li><strong>Vibescrobble.</strong> <em>Scrobble</em> writes a <code>com.vibescrobble.scrobble</code> record. The text must start with an emoji, for example <code>🚀 shipped the Cloudflare deploy</code>. Task is optional.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The page shows each round: the entry it called and the XRPC calls it made.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="cli">
		<h2>From your terminal</h2>
		<p>Connect the integration on the page first. The terminal uses that same session. You need <code>goat</code>, <code>curl</code> and <code>jq</code>.</p>
		<Code title="setup" code={cliSetup} />
		<h3>Path A: through your PDS</h3>
		<p>Your PDS signs a service-auth token and forwards the call. This is how any atproto app would call the site.</p>
		<Code code={viaProxy} />
		<h3>Path B: with a service-auth token</h3>
		<p>Fetch the token yourself and call the site directly. A token works once.</p>
		<Code code={viaToken} />
		<Diagram code={serviceAuth} label="Sequence of the two service-auth paths." />
	</section>

	<section id="own">
		<h2>Your own integration</h2>
		<p>
			Any OAuth client works as a record. Group scopes so people can grant them one at a time. The <code>client_id</code> and <code>redirect_uris</code> are placeholders; the site serves its own.
		</p>
		<Code title="example.json" code={ownRecord} />
		<Code code={ownPublish} />
		<p>To give it a module, see <a href="/modules">Write a module</a>.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="troubleshooting">
		<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
		<div class="table-scroll">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th>You see</th><th>Do this</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td>No integrations yet</td><td>Publish a record, then reload. The list reads your PDS each time.</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Module missing from a card</td><td>The module record's <code>session.uri</code> must name that integration. Republish with <code>publish-wasm.sh</code>.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>Service auth token was already used</code></td><td>Fetch a new token. Each <code>jti</code> works once.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>text must start with an emoji</code></td><td>Start the scrobble with an emoji.</td></tr>
					<tr><td>A run fails after you changed scopes</td><td>Press <em>Verify</em>, then reconnect with the groups the module needs.</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>
</Guide>
